@startuml
title ThingsBoard 3.6 Cassandra telemetry: registry, history, latest, TTL and async IO

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontColor #111827
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #253746
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #334155
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam participantBorderColor #334155
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam participantFontColor #111827
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF5CC
skinparam noteBorderColor #8A5A00
skinparam noteFontColor #111827
skinparam groupBorderColor #334155
skinparam groupHeaderBackgroundColor #E5E7EB
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam maxMessageSize 220

participant "Rule Engine Queue" as Queue
participant "TbMsgTimeseriesNode" as Node
participant "TelemetrySubscriptionService" as Telemetry
participant "BaseTimeseriesService" as Base
participant "Cassandra History DAO" as History
participant "Cassandra Latest DAO" as Latest
participant "Partition Cache" as Cache
participant "Buffered Rate Write Executor" as Buffer
participant "DataStax Driver" as Driver
database "Cassandra Replicas" as Cassandra
participant "WebSocket / Entity View" as Notify

== Rule Node entry ==
Queue -> Node : POST_TELEMETRY_REQUEST TbMsg
Node -> Node : parse TsKvEntry list\nresolve ttl and saveLatest flag
Node -> Telemetry : saveAndNotify(tenant, entity, entries, ttl, callback)
Telemetry -> Base : save(...) or saveWithoutLatest(...)

== Register three independent futures per datapoint ==
loop each TsKvEntry
  Base -> History : savePartition(entity, ts, key)
  Base -> History : save(entity, entry, ttl)
  opt saveLatest = true
    Base -> Latest : saveLatest(entity, entry)
  end
end
Base -> Base : Futures.allAsList(all mutations)

== Partition registry path ==
History -> History : partitionStart = truncate UTC timestamp
alt fixed INDEFINITE partitioning
  History --> Base : immediate null Future
else time buckets
  History -> Cache : has(entity,key,partition)?
  alt cache hit
    Cache --> History : true
    History --> Base : immediate success
  else cache miss or cache disabled
    History -> Buffer : INSERT ts_kv_partitions_cf\nTTL = system TTL only
  end
end

== History path ==
History -> History : effective TTL\nrequest or min(system, request)
History -> History : choose typed prepared statement
alt set_null_values_enabled
  History -> History : bind all typed cells\nnon-target cells = null
else target column only
  History -> History : old typed cells may remain
end
History -> Buffer : INSERT ts_kv_cf [USING TTL]

== Latest path ==
Latest -> Latest : bind entityType, entityId, key, payload ts, value
Latest -> Buffer : unconditional INSERT ts_kv_latest_cf\nno TTL and no payload-ts guard

== Buffered asynchronous IO ==
loop each CassandraStatementTask
  Buffer -> Buffer : tenant rate limit check
  alt rejected or bounded queue full
    Buffer --> Base : failed Future
  else queued
    Buffer -> Buffer : dispatcher checks approximate concurrency\nqueue+execution deadline
    Buffer -> Driver : session.executeAsync(statement with CL)
    Driver -> Cassandra : coordinator mutation
    alt write CL reached
      Cassandra --> Driver : AsyncResultSet
      Driver --> Buffer : completion on callback pool
      Buffer --> Base : success Future
      opt registry write succeeded
        Buffer -> Cache : put(entity,key,partition)
      end
    else timeout / unavailable / overload
      Cassandra --> Driver : failure
      Driver --> Buffer : exceptional completion
      Buffer --> Base : failed Future
    end
  end
end

== Combined result and notifications ==
alt every registered future succeeds
  Base --> Telemetry : success
  Telemetry -> Notify : publish latest/history update
  Telemetry --> Node : callback success
  Node --> Queue : Rule Node Success relation
else any future fails
  Base --> Telemetry : failed combination
  Telemetry --> Node : callback failure
  Node --> Queue : Rule Node Failure relation
end
note over History,Latest
  allAsList is not a Cassandra batch or transaction.
  Registry, history and latest mutations already applied are not rolled back.
end note

== Native history TTL versus latest lifetime ==
Cassandra -> Cassandra : history cells expire at effective TTL
Cassandra -> Cassandra : expired cells become tombstones\nphysical purge waits for compaction conditions
note over Cassandra,Latest
  Latest INSERT has no TTL. A last value can survive after all history expires.
end note

== Out-of-order latest overwrite ==
Queue -> Node : older payload ts arrives later
Node -> Latest : saveLatest(old payload timestamp)
Latest -> Buffer : ordinary INSERT same entity/key
Buffer -> Driver : executeAsync
Driver -> Cassandra : later write timestamp wins
note over Latest,Cassandra
  The payload ts column is not a compare condition.
  An older event submitted later can replace a newer latest value.
end note
@enduml
